    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0655" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.119/6–3050</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merchant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of Commerce</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Blaisdell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-30">June 30, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Tom</hi>: Confirming my telephone conversation
                    with you earlier today, it is the request of the Department of State that for
                    the time being action be suspended on export license applications for IB items
                    destined for mainland China now before you or which may be submitted and upon
                    which favorable action otherwise might be taken. The State Department
                    representative on the R–Procedure Committee has been instructed to take this
                    position.</p>
                <p>I am sure you understand the reasons for this request at this time. We will keep
                    in close touch with you on the matter.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Livingston</hi> T. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Merchant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
